# Generated Output Protection

See also `ai/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md` for the current pipeline.

## Never treat generated files as sources of truth

- Do **not** hand-edit `gmbinder/**` or `foundry/**/*.json` to correct campaign content.
- Edit `dawn-of-the-jedaii-campaign-guide.md` (primary authority), then regenerate when Kakeman89 authorizes a regen run.
- Output-only “fixes” will be lost on regeneration and create sync drift.

## Scripts

| Script | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| `tools/md_to_foundry_journal.py` | Reads primary guide → writes Foundry journal JSON |
| `tools/md_to_gmbinder.py` | Reads primary guide (+ external Koorivar file) → writes GM Binder Markdown |
| `tools/reorder_guide_chapters.py` | **Dangerous** — writes the primary guide in place |

- Do not execute write-capable scripts during audit sessions without explicit authorization.
- Do not mutate live Foundry worlds from the agent.
- Foundry page `_id` generation currently uses non-deterministic `secrets.choice`. Flag ID stability as a technical risk; do not “fix” IDs by hand-editing JSON unless Kakeman89 authorizes a tooling change.

## Generated-file notices

- Future GM Binder outputs should include a generated-file warning naming the authoritative source and regen tool.
- Foundry JSON cannot use comments; notice strategy (metadata / README / adjacent file) is deferred tooling work.
- Do **not** add generated-file notices during rules-only work unless separately authorized.

## Permissions

Keep the imported GM Guide journal **GM-only** by default. Player-safe material belongs in separately managed handouts (e.g. Appendix C), not by widening default journal ownership without authorization.
